Subject: [PATCH 03/23] =?UTF-8?q?feat(fast):=20service=5Ftier=20flex=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20one=20edit=20in=20the=20centralized=20tier=20table?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds flex (~50% cost saving on latency-tolerant workloads; OpenAI
https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/flex-processing, Gemini
https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/flex-inference) as a static tier:
one entry in agent.fast_mode's SERVICE_TIER_WORDS / STATIC_TIERS
(#128307's chokepoint — every surface parses through it), plus an
explicit flex branch in resolve_fast_mode_overrides next to ultrafast:
{"service_tier": "flex"} on OpenAI and tier-eligible Gemini models, None
on Anthropic (no flex equivalent — speed is a go-faster knob; mapping
flex onto it would silently bill MORE for a setting chosen to cost less)
and on Grok (xAI publishes no flex tier). The route gate is unchanged:
aggregator routes never receive first-party tier params, and two-level
aggregator ids stay tier-ineligible so /fast never confirms a tier it
cannot send. Gemini tier eligibility (2.5+, both tier docs' floor) joins
model_supports_fast_mode.

Closes #12700.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
